{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '2440,2505p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '4440,4475p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; rg -n 'attributed\\\\?|trace|fuel|cc3.*lane|tagged' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj src/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj | tail -75\"","aggregated_output":"                  (pr-str (walk/postwalk-replace renames source)))]\n    (apply str (map #(format \"%02x\" (bit-and 255 %))\n                    (.digest (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \"SHA-256\")\n                             (.getBytes payload \"UTF-8\"))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-kernel-canonical-source-hash\n  (testing \"fresh reads of pinned NBE source ignore reader gensym counters\"\n    (let [forms-a (read-forms 'latte_kernel.nbe)\n          forms-b (read-forms 'latte_kernel.nbe)\n          call '(latte-kernel.nbe/evaluation 'x)]\n      (is (not= (pr-str forms-a) (pr-str forms-b))\n          \"the regression actually exercises reader-generated symbols\")\n      (is (= (kernel-canonical-source-hash forms-a call)\n             (kernel-canonical-source-hash forms-b call)))))\n  (testing \"canonical names preserve symbol identity across forms and call\"\n    (doseq [[a b] '[[p1__123# p1__456#]\n                    [value__123__auto__ value__456__auto__]\n                    [G__123 G__456]]]\n      (is (= (kernel-canonical-source-hash [(list 'fn [a] a)] (list a))\n             (kernel-canonical-source-hash [(list 'fn [b] b)] (list b)))))\n    (is (not= (kernel-canonical-source-hash '[(fn [p1__123#] p1__123#)] '(p1__123#))\n              (kernel-canonical-source-hash '[(fn [p1__123#] p1__456#)] '(p1__123#)))\n        \"distinct generated symbols must remain distinct\")\n    (is (not= (kernel-canonical-source-hash '[(def x 1)] 'x)\n              (kernel-canonical-source-hash '[(def x 2)] 'x))\n        \"ordinary source edits still invalidate the hash\")))\n\n\n(defn- fresh-admission-run\n  \"Allocate ONE admission run, at the run composition (the top of an\n   evidence/binding run): a fresh scope supplied as plain data plus a\n   run-local ordinal allocator. Thread the returned run through\n   `kernel-row` / `kernel-compile` via the `-in-run` callers, which\n   assign DISTINCT ordinals within this run. Fresh runs call this\n   again and get distinct scopes; replay does NOT call this — it\n   explicitly re-supplies the retained run's scope+ordinal (or reuses\n   the retained compilation). No global counter: the atom is created\n   per run, held only by the run map the composition threads.\"\n  [label]\n  {:scope (str (name label) \"-\" (java.util.UUID/randomUUID))\n   :next-ordinal (atom 0)})\n\n\n(defn- admission-run-ordinal\n  [run]\n  (let [ordinal @(:next-ordinal run)]\n    (swap! (:next-ordinal run) inc)\n    ordinal))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-compile\n  \"Compile one oracle fixture under an explicit admission coordinate.\n\n   The admitting composition supplies `admission-scope` and the\n   per-scope `admission-ordinal` (both plain data); the batch token\n   of the admission origin `[:source :program batch-token j]` is the\n   pair `[admission-scope admission-ordinal]` and the member index\n   `j` is zero, because each admission here is a separately admitted\n   single-member batch — the ordinal therefore distinguishes\n   admissions through the token, and projected keys (reconstructed\n   from a single-member envelope, member index always zero) agree\n   with the recorded origin for every ordinal. Both coordinates are\n   recorded WHEN ADMITTING, before compilation, validated by the\n   same origin-shape rules as every source origin\n   (`vm/source-origin`), and retained with the compilation as\n  [dir]\n  (let [f (io/file dir)]\n    (if-not (.exists f)\n      0\n      (reduce + 0 (map (fn [x] (.length ^java.io.File x))\n                       (filter (fn [x] (.isFile ^java.io.File x))\n                               (file-seq f)))))))\n\n\n(defn- d1-heap-sampler!\n  \"Sample process used heap every interval-ms until stopped; stopping\n   answers the maximum observed. Process-wide JVM figures, a ceiling\n   measurement aid, not an object-graph census.\"\n  [interval-ms]\n  (let [running (atom true)\n        peak (atom 0)\n        sample (fn []\n                 (let [rt (Runtime/getRuntime)]\n                   (swap! peak max (- (.totalMemory rt) (.freeMemory rt)))))\n        thread (Thread. (fn []\n                          (try\n                            (while @running\n                              (sample)\n                              (Thread/sleep interval-ms))\n                            (catch Exception _ (sample)))))]\n    (.start thread)\n    {:stop! (fn []\n              (reset! running false)\n              (.join thread (long (* 5 interval-ms)))\n              (sample)\n              @peak)}))\n\n\n(defn- d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n  \"Exercise one live admission through a temporary file store and the\n   independent static gate; with opts, also run one mutated-input check\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:268:(defn attributed?\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:269:  \"Query one already-scoped fixture's table, bindings and complete lane traces.\nsrc/cljc/yang/correspondence_verifier.clj:299:   establish admission authenticity, executable-image derivations, trace\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:552:   stack trace is never compared).\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2017:(defn- kernel-trace-form\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2026:          trace-arity (fn [[params & body]]\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2030:                                 (list 'stream/put! 'gate-execution-trace\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2035:                        (trace-arity header) (map trace-arity header))))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2344:  \"One caller-site-tagged trace record `[fname arity caller-site]` against\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2390:   lane's trace ever records — a stale table after a fixture edit. The\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2406:  \"The ruled attribution query over `row`'s two caller-site-tagged C-lane\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2407:   traces: upstream `symbol` at arity `n` is credited when BOTH lanes\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2429:   without depending on the process's gensym counter. A trace evaluated\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2524:         program (into (into ['(def gate-execution-trace (stream/make 1000000))]\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2526:                       (concat (map kernel-trace-form forms) [call]))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2576:                    ref (get-in machine [:store 'gate-execution-trace])\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2579:                  (throw (ex-info \"Execution trace did not complete\" {:lane lane})))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3228:      ;; F2's bare traces into upstream /1 credit\") pinned the superseded\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3235:            (str \"F2 traces the ambient-tagged context entry at its stamped site: \" lane)))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3241:      ;; D1(a) accepted: a passing negative traces its head and credits directly.\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3250:   attribution over caller-site-tagged traces.\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3281:            \"a trace read against another fixture's canonical-source-hash refuses\")))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3393:       :reason \"Host stack traces have no portable error-data representation; the compiler refuses the accessor.\"}]\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3405:     :instruction-budget-note \"The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions. Body-entry stream writes add guest instructions; traced fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound. The harness drains only after halt. Under the D2 record lane the binding fixture's walker cell needs 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over 2M; semantic 1,105,792); the architect's 2026-11-04 ruling approves a uniform 4,000,000 acceptance budget (~1.98x headroom on the binding lane, measurement-supported, no per-fixture table). The attribution round's caller-site stamping adds one dispatcher call and one cell write per stamped guest call; every fixture in this evidence completed under the same 4,000,000 bound with the stamping active, and the trace stream bound stays stream/make 1000000 (one added field per body-entry record, no added records).\"\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3420:                :trace {:record-shape '[guest-function arity caller-site]\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3537:            (str \"Every credited path re-derives from both execution traces: \" [symbol n id])))\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3888:  ;; Bounds for this tagged run are recorded in the cc3 findings'\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3890:  ;; 4,000,000 guest instructions and 1,000,000 trace records per C\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4244:  ;; Static only: no instrumented machine or tagged trace is run here.\ntest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:4347:  ;; One static fixture only; no tagged execution and no independent verifier.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
